; docker/zones/climb.example.zone — CLIMB Phase 12
;
; Minimal authoritative zone for NSD-MTL serving.
; Hand-written (not generated from climb-dns) because:
;   - climb-dns generates wire-format DNS *messages*, not zone files
;   - climb-dns lacks SOA generation, zone-file presentation format, and
;     deterministic single-zone layout (records are randomized across 10 zones)
;   - A hand-written zone is the smallest correct path for Phase 12.3's "real zone"
;     requirement, per the investigation documented in the dev notes Phase 12.1
;
; This zone is unsigned. MTL RRSIGs require the verisign/mtl-mode-ldns signer
; (not yet vendored) — see the dev notes Phase 12.1 Blockers.

$ORIGIN climb.example.
$TTL 3600

@       IN  SOA     ns1.climb.example. hostmaster.climb.example. (
                    2026093001  ; serial
                    3600        ; refresh
                    900         ; retry
                    604800      ; expire
                    86400       ; minimum (negative-cache TTL)
)

@       IN  NS      ns1.climb.example.

; Apex A record (glue for ns1)
ns1     IN  A       127.0.0.1

; Sample host records — these are the records queried in Phase 12.5 verification
www     IN  A       10.0.0.1
www     IN  AAAA    2001:db8::1
mail    IN  A       10.0.0.2
mail    IN  MX  10  mx.climb.example.
api     IN  A       10.0.0.3
api     IN  TXT     "v=CLIMB-phase12"
mx      IN  A       10.0.0.4